# PR hygiene (always on)

Canonical policy: `docs/agent-efficiency/pr-review-cost-efficiency.md` · `docs/agent-efficiency/autonomous-pr-policy.md`

## Pre-PR critical self-review (mandatory — every PR)

**Before** the first push that opens a PR, and **before** every `ManagePullRequest create_pr` / PR update that ships new behavior, perform a **critical self-review** of the full diff against the requirement. Applies to **all** agent work — ad-hoc cloud agents, `/babysit`, `/babysit-plus`, `/execute-plan` workers, and humans using agents.

1. **Correctness & impact** — Happy paths, edge cases, error handling, regressions.
2. **Risks** — Security, data integrity, migrations, API contract drift, concurrency.
3. **Design quality** — Smallest change that meets intent; match repo patterns.
4. **Better solution** — Adopt a clearer/safer approach now; do not defer to review.
5. **Verification** — Run `./scripts/pre-push-changed.sh` after any adjustments.

Optional cost saver: `/review-bugbot` on the branch diff before push dedupes a paid Bugbot PR review when the patch is unchanged.

Only after this review passes: commit, push, create/update the PR.

## Automatic review (Bugbot-first)

- **Primary:** Cursor **Bugbot** on every PR (`Cursor Bugbot` check). Copilot is optional when credits are available.
- **Babysit wait:** Poll for **Bugbot**; do **not** halt on Copilot timeout when Bugbot + triage are complete. See autonomous-pr-policy §Automatic reviews.
- **Autofix:** **Off** — babysit+ owns triage and fixes (avoids double Cloud Agent spend).

## Model for PR babysitting

| Phase | Model |
|-------|--------|
| Implementation, architecture, large refactors | `composer-2.5` default; thinking models (e.g. Claude Sonnet) only when the task explicitly needs deep reasoning |
| **PR babysitting** (`/babysit`, `/babysit-plus`, post-PR triage, CI loop, merge) | **`composer-2.5` only** — never thinking/high models |

If the session model is not `composer-2.5` when starting babysit work, **stop and switch model** (Cursor dashboard → Models, or start a new cloud agent on `composer-2.5`) before triage, fixes, or merge steps.
